## Membership Level Computation

### Core class: `MembershipLevelResolver`
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/MembershipLevelResolver.java`

This is the single class that computes the membership level. The whole computation:

```java
8:  public final class MembershipLevelResolver {
10:     /** The highest level attainable on create; level 4 is reserved for tenure. */
11:     private static final int MAX_LEVEL = 3;
25:     public static int deriveMembershipLevel(String email, Integer namesakeCount) {
26:         int level = 1;
27:         if (email != null && !email.isBlank()) {
28:             level++;
29:         }
30:         if (namesakeCount != null && namesakeCount == 0) {
31:             level++;
32:         }
33:         return Math.min(level, MAX_LEVEL);
34:     }
35: }
```

Logic: starts at 1, +1 if email is present (non-blank), +1 if `namesakeCount == 0` (unique name at create time), capped at `MAX_LEVEL = 3`. Level 4 is documented as "reserved for tenure" but is NOT implemented anywhere in main code (see below).

### Where it is invoked

1. `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct expression that populates the DTO's `membershipLevel`:
```java
29: @Mapping(target = "membershipLevel",
30:     expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper.MembershipLevelResolver.deriveMembershipLevel(owner.getEmail(), owner.getNamesakeCount()))")
```

2. `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:178-180` — audit-log line on owner creation (same call, for logging only).

## Tenure / days / 365 / email

- Tenure and "365 days" / "level 4" appear ONLY in documentation/comments and the acceptance test, never in executable main logic:
  - `MembershipLevelResolver.java:10` comment: "level 4 is reserved for tenure."
  - `AcceptanceTest.java:7-9` comment: "level 4 requires tenure over 365 days."
- `email` feeds the level (+1 when non-blank), read via `owner.getEmail()`.
- The only `days` arithmetic in main code is unrelated to membership: `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:269` (`effective.plusDays(1)`) inside bulk-signup-warning logic.

## namesakeCount

- Field defined in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java:72-73` (`@Column(name = "namesake_count")`), getter/setter at lines 167-172.
- Computed at create by `OwnerRestControllerV1.countNamesakes(owner)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:325-332`: counts existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive), before the new owner is saved (so 0 = unique). Set at line 203.

## Household

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/HouseholdResolver.java` — `deriveHouseholdId(lastName, postcode)` (lines 26-29): SHA-256 hex prefix of normalized lastName + `|` + postcode.
- `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:
  - `assignHouseholdId(Owner)` lines 464-471.
  - `requireHouseholdNotDuplicate` (household duplicate guard) around lines 490-495.
  - `populateHouseholdMemberCount(Owner)` lines 508-518 — counts owners sharing the same `householdId` (household of 1 when null); sets transient `householdMemberCount`.
- `Owner.java:70` (`householdId` field), lines 159-164 getter/setter; the household-member-count transient field is documented near line 86.
- Household is also part of the identity key (`IdentityKeyResolver.java:31-47`) and duplicate-key advice (`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java:248,262`).

## Test files

There is NO dedicated unit test for `MembershipLevelResolver` (no `MembershipLevelResolverTest`, no household/namesake unit tests). Membership level is covered only by one acceptance test:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
```java
7:  /** tenure-cap: level 4 requires tenure over 365 days, so a brand-new owner (zero tenure)
8:   * never exceeds level 3. A new owner with an email and no namesake maxes the pre-tenure factors,
9:   * and must land at level 3, not 4. */
10: class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
12:     @Test
13:     void coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3() throws Exception {
14:         ObjectNode o = withPostcode(ownerNode());
15:         o.put("email", uniqueEmail());
16:         int id = createOwnerOk(o);
17:         getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.membershipLevel").value(3));
18:     }
19: }
```

Its harness/helpers (`ownerNode`, `withPostcode`, `uniqueEmail`, `createOwnerOk`, `getOwner`) live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`.

### Summary
The membership-level computation is fully contained in `MembershipLevelResolver.deriveMembershipLevel` (email + unique-name factors, capped at 3). Level 4 / tenure / 365-day logic is described in comments and asserted-as-absent by the acceptance test, but is not implemented in the codebase. Only the acceptance test exercises membership level; there is no unit test for the resolver itself.

